> Yes. My best advice is: start someplace else.

Check.  A glance at the files say they are *.c in the src directory
and *.h in the includes directory.  If you're at a point where you
can't glance at a directory listing and tell it isn't C++ you're
far too early in the learning process to dive in that deep.  Learn
to ride a bicycle before you learn to drive an 18-wheeler.  Nethack
is great for college junior/senior level not for your current state.
Start here and you will waste your time getting confused when you
should be learning the basics.  Yes, it is always tempting to do
stuff out of order.  Resist that temptation right now.  Read some
of the basic texts on what is involved in programming, learn some
of the basic principles (the type of principle that have zero to
do with what language it's in), learn a couple of the easy
languages like v-basic and pascal.  Then you'll be ready to enter
the world of C and the world of group practice.  Right now you
are working on diagramming sentences so you shouldn't be trying to
join the college debate team.  That time will come sooner than you
think, but only if you avoid the temptation this year.

